From dca89dc2d948512677ceb5370efc312a6ec3a069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 03:17:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0190: Discovered Quests split into its own tab, with nav
 shimmer

Pulled quest chains out of the Quest Board tab (previously a section
at the bottom of a hero's own Contracts list) into their own tab,
registered next to Quests in the Adventure group.

- Exported ChainQuestBanner/QuestCard/QuestCardProps/Offer/HeroTab
  from QuestPanel.tsx for reuse rather than duplicating them
- New DiscoveredQuestsPanel.tsx: own hero-tab selection state, same
  QuestCard rendering, same per-hero reqLevel filter the old
  chainOffers computation used
- Removed the old chainOffers logic and render block from
  QuestPanel.tsx entirely; updated its tooltip
- New chainQuestAvailable boolean in attention.ts's shared
  AttentionCounts (true when any hero meets any chain offer's
  reqLevel), driving a rotating border-light on the new tab's nav
  button (.chain-available in app.css) instead of a numeric badge

No changes to quest chain data, discovery, or QuestManager -- pure UI
relocation plus one new derived signal and its CSS.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build --config
vite.web.config.ts both pass clean.
